@startuml dedup-supersession-materialize
!theme plain
title Dedup/supersession + materialize — data flow (logical parts, not functions)

component "Producer" as Producer
folder "Transport\n.local-artifacts/review/" as Transport
component "Consumer validate" as Validate
database "Dedup/supersession index\nimported/" as Index
component "Consumer materialize" as Materialize
folder "materialized output\nmaterialized/<messageId>/" as Output
component "git checkout\n(cwd)" as Git
actor "review-agent" as ReviewAgent

' --- Publish side ---
Producer --> Transport : publish A1 (context_snapshot)
Producer --> Transport : publish A2\n(supersedesMessageId = A1)

' --- Validate side ---
Transport --> Validate : message.json\n(A1, then A2)

Validate --> Index : write <messageId>.json (sha256)\nimported/A1.json\nimported/A2.json
Validate --> Index : A2: follow supersession chain\n(missing parent / cycle /\nconcurrent successor)

' --- Materialize side ---
Validate --> Materialize : validated context\n(baseOid, headOid, ...)
Materialize --> Git : run git in cwd\nverify OIDs (cat-file -e)\ngit diff base..head
Git --> Materialize : base..head diff

Materialize --> Output : diff.patch\ndiffstat.txt\ncommits.txt

' --- Review side ---
Output --> ReviewAgent : read materialized diff\n+ validated context
ReviewAgent --> ReviewAgent : produce findings

note bottom of Index
  Index writes are ATOMIC (temp + rename)
  so supersession_check's glob never
  reads a half-written file.
end note

note bottom of Output
  Output is PER-REVIEW:
  materialized/<messageId>/ (not a
  single fixed dir) — concurrent agents
  on one home do not collide.
end note
@enduml
